rs/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-15T19:54:03Z","updated_at":"2026-07-15T19:59:27Z","body":"Tested this PR locally ~and I didn't really get the need for this (without display frame)~ I guess device frame can be implemented seperately.\r\n\r\n- Can you remove duplicates? There's devices with exact same resolution (iPhone 17 and iPhone 17 Pro, Galaxy S26+ and Galaxy S26 Ultra, etc.)\r\n- How exactly `safe_area` affects the final view? `DisplayServer.get_display_safe_area()` doesn't return those values. I didn't understand how it works (haven't looked at code yet).\r\n- why there's no safearea defined (by default) for Android devices?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4984711504/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4990499968","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111787#issuecomment-4990499968","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111787","id":4990499968,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKXT8gA","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-16T09:52:31Z","updated_at":"2026-07-16T09:52:56Z","body":"I didn't review thoroughly but some more obvious usability suggestions:\r\n- I would consider setting all resolution preset options to 'disabled' (faded, unclickable) when Stretch to Fit is enabled, thus making the relationship between the embedded window mode and the resolution presets much clearer. Right now the relationship between the two groups is unclear and messy.\r\n- This device list will be high-maintenance, requiring yearly updating. Are we sure about this?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4990499968/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5186423634","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111787#issuecomment-5186423634","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111787","id":5186423634,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNSKLUg","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T01:19:04Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T01:19:04Z","body":"> * This device list will be high-maintenance, requiring yearly updating. Are we sure about this?\r\n\r\n@AdriaandeJongh We touched on this in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111787/changes#r3581508008; so long as we keep the list small (drop older devices when adding new ones), and have a consistent source for the data, the maintenance should not be an issue. Android and iOS already update at least once a year due to new SDK requirements, we can make this list part of the update.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5186423634/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5186803871","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111787#issuecomment-5186803871","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111787","id":5186803871,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNShYnw","user":{"login":"ajreckof","id":66184050,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MTg0MDUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66184050?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof","html_url":"https://github.com/ajreckof","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T02:22:52Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T02:22:52Z","body":"I did not look at the code or test it yet but here are my usability suggestions:\r\n- I feel like the list is huge and makes it harder to find the one you are looking for, so when you don't actually plan to export to this becomes a huge list taking space for nothing. \r\n- I feel like this should not appear as long as i don't have an export template that makes sense for it. (ie. if i don't have iOS export, i don't have the iphones resolutions). Either those would automatically detected from export or you would be able to turn them on off manually. Maybe a mix of the two with a on/default/off option with default option detecting export.\r\n- maybe to reduce the size of the list they could be nested inside a sub-menu per platform.\r\n- I would include more brand especially those that can come with a pre-installed open source OS, also we could also add options for desktop -> macos as a really limited number of options. For linux we could have steamDeck\r\n- I think we should directly let EditorExportPlugin add new ones which would reduce the need for adding more as defaults.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5186803871/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]